Since people tend to put in future nethack suggestions here, I've
created a list of some things I'd like to see in Nethack in future version(s)...

- The selective pickup option as described previously on numerous
  occasions.

- Make it so you can no longer wish for the more powerful artifacts.
  (ie: Mjollnir, Excalibur, Stormbringer ).  Maybe give you a ordinary
  war hammer/longsword/broad sword.  You should only be able to attain
  these items through the normal channels (ie:sacrifice).
  Perhaps make these guys have a 'personality'...

- Add a brief note on the artifacts into the 'data' file so that if you
  use the '/' command to id it, it'll tell you something about that
  particular artifact ( at least part of the myth surrounding it )  This
  already exists for the Orcrist and Snickersnee artifacts, the rest
  should be added.

- a scroll of identify should be able to identify whether or not an item
  is corrosion resistant.

- gems to play a more important role with perhaps some more magical ones
  added ( ie: ones that confer fire resistance,clairavoyance,
  searching/see invisible(gem of true seeing) whether just by having or
  by using ) Perhaps ones that can cast a 'one shot' spell (thus making
  the gem useless glass) like a light or healing spell.  

- They should create a magic lantern that uses gems as lenses and can cast
  a certain spell depending on the type of gem contained therein from 
  nothing for a piece of glass to perhaps a wish with a dilythium
  crystal (this would double as a destructive way to identify gems, like
  reading a scroll, quaffing a potion, or dropping rings down a sink ). A
  cursed lantern would blow up, and using a cursed gem would give a chance
  of the lantern exploding as well or causing bad spells to be cast...

- make it so that all items are required to make saving throws for
  polymorphing as well as creatures.  This will help curtail extensive use
  of polypiling as the item polymorphed could very well be destroyed in
  the process.  Items already have to do a form of this when you are hit
  by a bolt of fire/cold/electricity... (your potion of gain level boils
  and explodes!)

- shopkeepers should prevent monsters from stealing from their shops as
  well as you.  Imagine the wandering nymph picking up a ring from the
  shop... She teleports out and off goes the alarm!  The keystone kops
  are after the nymph! (peaceful towards you though) They then proceed
  to beat the nymph to a pulp (but not before she charms a few of them
  out of their rubber hoses >8), and cream pies)... When she's dead they
  go back where they came from.

- make musical instruments play (pun) a more important role.  Already
  there's a horn of cold/fire and magic whistle... add more with other
  abilities (iether conveying an intrinsic or permiting the casting of
  spells).  Add a bard character class (well (m)usician so as not to
  take away the (b)arbarian )

- add some class specific items to the dungeon that only a certain class
  can use  (ie: holy items for priest, thiefly tools for rogues, magical
  paraphernelia for the wizards, et al, just so much dead weight for
  those none in the appropriate class(es) )

- more character classes! (one per letter would be fun)
  I especially liked the demon class mentioned a while back (from lowly
  manes to mighty demon prince!)

- a way to create a 'site'. ie: a sink, fountain, alter.  The
  ability to do this would have to be VERY limited.

- ability to gain some of the class specific intrinsics like the
  archaelogist gem identifying or priests detecting of curses/blessings.
  Perhaps a detect evil for curses, detect good for blessings (two
  different intrinsics)

- some new wands:  wand of paralysis - similar to the wand of sleep
  except that monsters imobilized with it can not be 'woken' up
  by any noises (ie:whistles,kicking doors,explosions, et al)
  Could then add a paralysis resistance intrinsic.
	wand of wonder - this would be an extremely fun item that has
  a random chance (perhaps with some of the chances weighted a bit) of
  acting like any other wand when zapped (from a wand of nothing to a 
  wand of wishing), perhaps with a few specialized occurances as well
  (perhaps emulating read scrolls, or creating sites
  (ie:sinks,fountains) occassionaly with a cursed effect (more likely
  if the wand itself is cursed)

- an item or ability (ie:for rogues) to create traps, perhaps also
  requiring components (ie:teleport scrolls to create teleport traps (or
  rings?) )

- potions of fire/cold/sleep/poison/electricity/etc resistance.  These
  would act as temporary protection for the unprotected.

- a new special water level.  Perhaps a large underground lake?
  Would allow the addition of many aquatic-type baddies (sea dragons,
  kraken,mermen/maids,syrens,sharks, et al)
  Add two new intrinsics: swim - allow person to cross over water
  squares (great for pools!) but acts much like levitation in that you
  can not pick up anything in the water on the bottom as you are
  swimming along the surface...
		amphibiousness - allow person to breath underwater as
  well as out of the water (basicaly walk along the bottom)
  Person would be 'slowed' unless possesing both of these intrinsics.
  Add water breathing and swimming spells..
  New items could be potion/ring of water breathing,gauntlets of
  swimming,swim suit, inflatable dinghies (sort of like a figurine in
  that you can only apply it once than it's too big to carry...),
  water wings, scuba suits, flippers, mask&snorkels, harpoons,
  water-proof bags (to hold scrolls or you'd end up with lots of blank
  paper and rusty daggers), water crystals.
  Thrown weapons could have a smaller range (unless harpoon)
  Spells could act differently underwater (ie:no fire,
  cold could freeze a square of water solid(with monster in it!))
  Maybe a named trident artifact.
  Have small 'islands' with special sites on them (altars,fountains).
  A (s)ailor character class - starting with swim, cutlas, potion of
     booze(rum),oranges(scurvy),etc.., god could be Poseidon
  Whirlpools that suck you under to a fountain one level down...
  or geysers that toss you one level up...
  The potential is enourmous...

- a eye glasses tool item ( as mentioned previously ) with magical and
  non-magical types. (the Peril sensitive glasses would be
  especially fun!, or diving masks, reflective sunglasses, et al)

- a (l)ook command that allows you to type 'l' then a direction and it
  will tell you everything you see in your line of sight until you hit a
  wall or other barrier.  Does not convey specifics about items, but can
  be used to tell the type of tool (ie:lamp,figurine,pick-axe) or armour
  (ie:boots,helmet) etc...  Will only convey the top item in a pile 
  (though it should tell you there's a pile of stuff)

just some thoughts.... (comments?)

Aaron.
